ORBITAL-TILING(7)          TriadicFrameworks Manual          ORBITAL-TILING(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-tiling - resonance-tiling kernels, temporal Voronoi tiling, and
                        constellation-scale tile fusion for SAR constellations

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital tiling defines:
           • resonance-tiling kernels
           • temporal Voronoi tiling
           • harmonic-aware tile segmentation
           • constellation-scale tile fusion
           • tile-based sweep and maneuver planning

DESCRIPTION
       orbital-tiling describes how RTT partitions orbital time into structured
       resonance-time tiles. These tiles act as the fundamental units of
       temporal planning, enabling sweep placement, Δv scheduling, and
       constellation-scale coordination based on resonance density, harmonic
       phase, and timing-grid geometry.

       Tiling enables:
           • multi-resolution temporal segmentation
           • resonance-aware sweep placement
           • harmonic-phase partitioning
           • constellation-scale tile fusion
           • predictive tile evolution across cycles

       WRSADC uses tiling as the substrate for grid fusion, choreography, and
       timing architectures.

RESONANCE-TILING KERNELS
       Resonance-tiling kernels generate tiles based on resonance envelope
       structure.

       Kernel inputs:
           • envelope amplitude R(t)
           • spectral density S(f,t)
           • gradient polarity G(t)
           • harmonic-lock stability H(t)
           • timing-grid nodes

       Kernel types:

           amplitude kernel
                  Tiles based on envelope amplitude peaks.

           spectral kernel
                  Tiles based on spectral density clusters.

           gradient kernel
                  Tiles based on gradient polarity transitions.

           harmonic kernel
                  Tiles based on harmonic-phase boundaries.

           hybrid kernel
                  Combines amplitude, spectral, and harmonic criteria.

       Kernel output:
           • tile boundaries
           • tile density classification
           • tile ancestry metadata

EXAMPLE: RESONANCE-TILING KERNEL
       Envelope amplitude R(t) over one orbital period T:

           Peaks at: 12 min, 54 min, 78 min

       Kernel output tiles:
           [0–12], [12–30], [30–54], [54–70], [70–78], [78–96]

       Tile density:
           • high: [10–14], [52–56], [76–80]
           • medium: adjacent tiles
           • low: remaining tiles

       Result:
           • sweeps placed in high-density tiles
           • Δv triads in medium-density tiles
           • drift correction in low-density tiles

TEMPORAL VORONOI TILING
       Temporal Voronoi tiling partitions orbital time based on proximity to
       resonance or harmonic “sites.”

       Site types:
           • resonance peaks
           • harmonic-phase nodes
           • sync nodes
           • maneuver nodes

       Voronoi region definition:
           A tile contains all times closer to its site than to any other site.

       Voronoi tiling types:

           resonance Voronoi
                  Sites = envelope peaks.

           harmonic Voronoi
                  Sites = harmonic-phase nodes.

           sync Voronoi
                  Sites = constellation sync nodes.

           hybrid Voronoi
                  Sites = union of resonance + harmonic + sync nodes.

EXAMPLE: TEMPORAL VORONOI TILING
       Sites over one orbital period T:

           resonance peaks: 15, 60
           harmonic nodes: 30, 90

       Voronoi tiles:
           [0–15], [15–30], [30–60], [60–90], [90–T]

       Result:
           • sweeps at 15 and 60
           • Δv triads at 30 and 90
           • drift correction in outer tiles

HARMONIC-PHASE TILE OVERLAYS
       Harmonic-phase overlays subdivide tiles based on harmonic-phase cycles.

       Overlay variables:
           • harmonic ratio n:m
           • phase alignment φ_harm
           • lock stability index L_harm

       Overlay types:

           integer overlay
                  Tiles subdivided at integer harmonic boundaries.

           rational overlay
                  Tiles subdivided at rational harmonic boundaries.

           nested overlay
                  Harmonic subdivisions inside resonance tiles.

           resonance-harmonic overlay
                  Harmonic boundaries aligned to resonance peaks.

EXAMPLE: HARMONIC-PHASE OVERLAY
       Tile: [0–30]
       Harmonic ratio: 3:2

       Subdivision:
           [0–12], [12–20], [20–30]

       Result:
           • sweeps at 12 and 20
           • Δv triads at 30
           • stable harmonic-lock

CONSTELLATION-SCALE TILE FUSION
       Tile fusion merges tiles across platforms into a unified constellation
       tiling.

       Fusion layers:

           1. timing-grid alignment
           2. resonance-density alignment
           3. harmonic-phase alignment
           4. sync-field alignment

       Fusion output:

           • constellation sweep tiles
           • constellation Δv tiles
           • constellation sync tiles
           • constellation resonance windows

       Fusion modes:

           synchronous fusion
                  All platforms share identical tiles.

           harmonic fusion
                  Tiles aligned via harmonic ratios.

           braided fusion
                  Tiles interleave across platforms.

           mesh fusion
                  Distributed tile fusion across constellation nodes.

EXAMPLE: CONSTELLATION TILE FUSION
       Platforms A, B, C:

           A tiles: [0–20], [20–40], [40–60]
           B tiles: [0–30], [30–60]
           C tiles: [10–25], [25–50], [50–60]

       Fused constellation tiles:
           [0–10], [10–20], [20–25], [25–30], [30–40], [40–50], [50–60]

       Result:
           • sweeps at 20, 40, 60
           • Δv triads at 30 and 50
           • constellation sync at 10 and 25

TILING FAILURE MODES
       Tiling may degrade due to:

           • tile fragmentation
           • resonance tile collapse
           • harmonic-phase misalignment
           • Voronoi boundary drift
           • constellation tile mismatch

       Diagnostic indicators:

           tiling-integrity score
           tilemap fragmentation
           overlay deviation
           sync-index drop
           sweep-tile error

       WRSADC halts unsafe tiling states.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:

           • tile boundaries
           • tile densities
           • Voronoi regions
           • harmonic overlays
           • constellation tile fusion history

       Lineage enables long-term tiling forecasting.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes resonance-tiling kernels
           • generates Voronoi tilings
           • overlays harmonic-phase grids
           • fuses constellation tiles
           • schedules sweeps and maneuvers
           • blocks unsafe tiling states

       WRSADC is the tiling conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital tiling transforms SAR constellations into tessellated
       resonance-time systems. Resonance kernels, Voronoi tiling, and
       constellation-scale tile fusion ensure that sweep choreography,
       harmonic-lock, and multi-agent synchronization remain stable across
       long mission timelines.

